    outline:
      - when: Week 1
        topic: Algorithms with numbers — arithmetic and modular arithmetic
      - when: Week 2
        topic: Primality testing, cryptography, and universal hashing; divide and conquer begins with multiplication and recurrences
      - when: Week 3
        topic: Mergesort, medians, matrix multiplication, and the fast Fourier transform; depth-first search and strongly connected components
      - when: Week 4
        topic: Paths in graphs — breadth-first search and Dijkstra's algorithm; greedy algorithms — spanning trees, Huffman encoding, set cover
      - when: Week 5
        topic: Midterm exam; dynamic programming — longest increasing subsequence, edit distance, knapsack
      - when: Week 6
        topic: NP-complete problems and reductions; coping with NP-completeness — exhaustive search, approximation, local search
